          <p>
            If you are unsure where to start, put the shake wherever your current day has the biggest protein gap, usually breakfast or the afternoon. Then make sure your other meals each include a solid serving of protein, such as a palm-sized portion of meat or fish, a cup of Greek yogurt or a few eggs. That covers nearly everything the timing research has to offer.
          </p>

          <p>
            Product choice matters a little for timing. Whey and whey isolate digest quickly and suit post-workout and morning use; casein digests slowly and suits the evening; plant blends work anywhere but may need a slightly larger serving to match the leucine in whey. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder/">best protein powder</a> rankings and <a href="/best-whey-protein-isolate/">whey isolate picks</a> list third-party tested options in each category.
